 "why": "audit I1 (runs/pt6v2/tests/audit_v7_result_20261122.md): V7 leaves the torus / box5 lines out and the row's text grows to the left, so dim's slot-1 share goes 0.50 -> ~0.75 after the drop; the domain eval question is always in slot 1, so F109's '77% retained' may be inflated by the slot shift. V7b replaces each dropped line in its slot by a same-length text filler: every kept line keeps the flag-off (registered all6) positions and slots; total text tokens = V7's.",
 "reading_rule": "Report S_b with its CI and the paired slot effect; if the slot effect's CI includes 0 and S_b's CI includes 0.77, F109's 77% stands and its qualifier 2 is replaced by the measured slot effect; otherwise the paper's 77% is replaced by S_b. No check gates the read-out.",
